{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1150,1220p;1230,1290p;760,840p'\"","aggregated_output":"   760\t\n   761\t\n   762\t(defn- ingress-gaps\n   763\t  [state]\n   764\t  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n   765\t     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)\n   766\t     (:ingress-gaps (:observer (:indexer state)) 0)))\n   767\t\n   768\t\n   769\t(defn- consume-failed-round\n   770\t  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n   771\t\n   772\t   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n   773\t   observers resumes from the session the throw carried — the failing\n   774\t   stage's, matched by the medium it holds — or from where the round began\n   775\t   when it carried none, and reads past every batch still on its medium.\n   776\t   The shell is the only appender and appends one batch per round, so what\n   777\t   remains is the failed batch alone.  The VM is the one the round began\n   778\t   with, so a half-run continuation cannot be resumed — and its error\n   779\t   replayed — by the next input.  Output the round already emitted is\n   780\t   drained here, once.\"\n   781\t  [state error]\n   782\t  (let [carried (get-in (ex-data error) [:session :observer])\n   783\t        resume (fn [observer]\n   784\t                 (if (and observer\n   785\t                          carried\n   786\t                          (= (:stream carried) (:stream observer)))\n   787\t                   carried\n   788\t                   observer))\n   789\t        drained (assoc state\n   790\t                       :observer (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n   791\t                       :row-observer (drain-observer\n   792\t                                       (resume (:row-observer state)))\n   793\t                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state)))\n   794\t        [state' output-text]\n   795\t        (drain-output\n   796\t          (cond-> drained\n   797\t            (> (ingress-gaps drained) (ingress-gaps state))\n   798\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n   799\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n   800\t\n   801\t\n   802\t(defn- run-index-stage\n   803\t  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n   804\t   forwarded packet as one transaction and publishes the covered indexes.\n   805\t   It runs before the evaluator, so a program is indexed whether its VM\n   806\t   returns, parks, or raises; the two observers meet only at the medium.\"\n   807\t  [state]\n   808\t  (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n   809\t\n   810\t\n   811\t(defn- run-expander-stage\n   812\t  \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n   813\t   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n   814\t   failed expansion forwards nothing, yet its cursor advances (yin.vm.macro.md\n   815\t   decision 12).  Returns the state with the expander's progress and the\n   816\t   drained `{:errors :forwarded}` summary.\"\n   817\t  [state]\n   818\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n   819\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n   820\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n   821\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n   822\t\n   823\t\n   824\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n   825\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n   826\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n   827\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n   828\t   the other.\"\n   829\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n   830\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n   831\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n   832\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n   833\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n   834\t                                load-program\n   835\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n   836\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n   837\t\n   838\t\n   839\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n   840\t  [errors]\n  1150\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n  1151\t\n  1152\t   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n  1153\t   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n  1154\t   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n  1155\t  [state program]\n  1156\t  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n  1157\t    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1158\t    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n  1159\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n  1160\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n  1161\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n  1162\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n  1163\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n  1164\t        (let [expanded (try\n  1165\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n  1166\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1167\t                                   :clj Exception\n  1168\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n  1169\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n  1170\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n  1171\t            failed\n  1172\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n  1173\t                  expanded (cond-> expanded\n  1174\t                             (pos? forwarded) run-index-stage)]\n  1175\t              (cond\n  1176\t                (> (ingress-gaps expanded) (ingress-gaps state'))\n  1177\t                [(assoc expanded :ingress-loss? true)\n  1178\t                 (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1179\t\n  1180\t                (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state expanded)\n  1181\t\n  1182\t                :else [(assoc expanded :vm (:vm state))\n  1183\t                       (format-expansion-errors errors)]))))))))\n  1184\t\n  1185\t\n  1186\t(defn- compile-clojure-forms\n  1187\t  [forms]\n  1188\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n  1189\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n  1190\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n  1191\t\n  1192\t\n  1193\t(defn- compile-source\n  1194\t  [lang input]\n  1195\t  (case lang\n  1196\t    :clojure (compile-clojure-forms (read-forms input))\n  1197\t    :python (yang.python/compile input)\n  1198\t    :php (yang.php/compile input)\n  1199\t    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported Yin REPL language\" {:lang lang}))))\n  1200\t\n  1201\t\n  1202\t(defn- compile-command-ast\n  1203\t  [state arg]\n  1204\t  (case (:lang state)\n  1205\t    :clojure (if (string? arg)\n  1206\t               (compile-source :clojure arg)\n  1207\t               (yang.clojure/compile arg))\n  1208\t    (if (string? arg)\n  1209\t      (compile-source (:lang state) arg)\n  1210\t      (throw (ex-info \"This compile command expects a source string\"\n  1211\t                      {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n  1212\t\n  1213\t\n  1214\t(defn- render-compile-output\n  1215\t  \"Render the frontend syntax, the input row batch, and what the session's\n  1216\t   expander would make of it against its current store: the expanded tree\n  1217\t   packet (or the expansion error) and the event rows.  The expansion is a\n  1218\t   preview; its context is discarded, so nothing is committed.\"\n  1219\t  [state ast]\n  1220\t  (let [batch (encoder/program-batch ast)\n  1230\t\n  1231\t(defn- rebuild-session\n  1232\t  \"Replace the VM, the expander, and their media, attachments, and\n  1233\t   observers.  The value history is cleared with them: a closure in `*1`\n  1234\t   names a code segment the old VM held, which the new one does not.  The\n  1235\t   new expander holds only the standard forms.  A require still pending\n  1236\t   on the old VM is dropped with it: its link pair is the session's, and\n  1237\t   the new session answers from its own.\"\n  1238\t  [state vm-type]\n  1239\t  (merge state\n  1240\t         (make-session vm-type (:output-stream state)\n  1241\t                       (:extra-primitives state)\n  1242\t                       (:shell-token state)\n  1243\t                       (:index-store state))\n  1244\t         {:vm-type vm-type\n  1245\t          :ingress-loss? false\n  1246\t          :last-value nil\n  1247\t          :last-value-2 nil\n  1248\t          :last-value-3 nil\n  1249\t          :pending-run nil}))\n  1250\t\n  1251\t\n  1252\t(declare repl-state)\n  1253\t\n  1254\t\n  1255\t(defn handle-command\n  1256\t  \"Answer one shell command.  Unsupported arguments are answered as text, not\n  1257\t   thrown, so a mistyped command cannot end a step.\"\n  1258\t  [state form]\n  1259\t  (let [[command & args] form]\n  1260\t    (case command\n  1261\t      vm (let [vm-type (first args)]\n  1262\t           (if (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n  1263\t             [(rebuild-session state vm-type)\n  1264\t              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type) \" (store cleared)\")]\n  1265\t             [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL VM type \" (pr-str vm-type)\n  1266\t                         \"; supported: \"\n  1267\t                         (pr-str (vec (keys vm-constructors))))]))\n  1268\t      lang (let [lang (first args)]\n  1269\t             (if (contains? lang-labels lang)\n  1270\t               [(assoc state :lang lang)\n  1271\t                (str \"Switched to \" (get lang-labels lang))]\n  1272\t               [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL language \" (pr-str lang)\n  1273\t                           \"; supported: \" (pr-str (vec (keys lang-labels))))]))\n  1274\t      compile [state (render-compile-output\n  1275\t                       state\n  1276\t                       (compile-command-ast state (first args)))]\n  1277\t      reset [(rebuild-session state (:vm-type state))\n  1278\t             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n  1279\t      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n  1280\t      help [state help-text]\n  1281\t      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n  1282\t      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n  1283\t      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n  1284\t      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n  1285\t\n  1286\t\n  1287\t(defn- eval-parsed*\n  1288\t  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n  1289\t   re-check.\"\n  1290\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.index-test\n     2\t  \"The shell's code indexer (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md): a\n     3\t   dao.space.index observer on program-out, one transaction per forwarded\n     4\t   program, covered indexes published into dao.jing each round.\"\n     5\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n     6\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     7\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n     8\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n     9\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    10\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    11\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    12\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    13\t            [yin.repl.index :as repl.index]\n    14\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    15\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]))\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\t(defn- stream-values\n    19\t  \"Every value currently on a stream, read from its oldest cursor.\"\n    20\t  [s]\n    21\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n    22\t         acc []]\n    23\t    (let [r (stream/next s cursor)]\n    24\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    25\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    26\t        acc))))\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn- transactions\n    30\t  \"The atomic transaction records the session's indexer committed.\"\n    31\t  [state]\n    32\t  (mapv :dao.space/transaction\n    33\t        (stream-values (get-in state [:indexer :transactor :local-stream]))))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- evaluate\n    37\t  [state lines]\n    38\t  (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\n    39\t            (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\n    40\t              [state' (conj texts text)]))\n    41\t          [state []]\n    42\t          lines))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(def ^:private ref-attrs\n    46\t  (into #{}\n    47\t        (keep (fn [[a spec]] (when (= :db.type/ref (:db/valueType spec)) a)))\n    48\t        vm/schema))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn- modulo-ids\n    52\t  \"`[e a v]` of `datoms` with entity ids relabelled by first appearance, so\n    53\t   two projections of one tree compare equal whatever ids they minted.\"\n    54\t  [datoms]\n    55\t  (let [ids (into {}\n    56\t                  (map-indexed (fn [i e] [e i]))\n    57\t                  (distinct (map first datoms)))\n    58\t        relabel (fn [a v]\n    59\t                  (cond (not (contains? ref-attrs a)) v\n    60\t                        (vector? v) (mapv ids v)\n    61\t                        :else (ids v)))]\n    62\t    (mapv (fn [[e a v]] [(ids e) a (relabel a v)]) datoms)))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(deftest one-program-is-one-transaction-of-its-expanded-projection\n    66\t  (let [state (repl/create-state)\n    67\t        [state' result] (repl/eval-input state \"(+ 1 2)\")\n    68\t        [packet] (stream-values (:row-stream state'))\n    69\t        root (first packet)\n    70\t        rows (:rows (macro/packet->row-set packet))\n    71\t        txs (transactions state')\n    72\t        {:keys [t datoms]} (first txs)\n    73\t        meta-e (some (fn [[e a]] (when (= :db/op a) e)) datoms)\n    74\t        meta-facts (filterv #(= meta-e (first %)) datoms)\n    75\t        addresses (filterv #(= :yin/address (second %)) datoms)\n    76\t        ast-facts (filterv #(and (not= meta-e (first %))\n    77\t                                 (not= :yin/address (second %)))\n    78\t                           datoms)]\n    79\t    (is (= \"3\" result) \"the evaluator's answer is unchanged\")\n    80\t    (is (= 1 (count txs)) \"exactly one transaction for the program\")\n    81\t    (testing \"its datoms are ast->datoms of the expanded tree, modulo ids\"\n    82\t      (is (= (modulo-ids (vm/ast->datoms (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n    83\t                                           (macro/packet->row-set packet))))\n    84\t             (modulo-ids ast-facts))))\n    85\t    (testing \"the transactor allocated t; every datom carries it\"\n    86\t      (is (integer? t))\n    87\t      (is (every? #(= t (nth % 3)) datoms)))\n    88\t    (testing \"e is transactor-local, with :yin/address back to the row\"\n    89\t      (is (every? #(and (integer? (first %)) (<= 16 (first %))) datoms))\n    90\t      (is (= (set (map first ast-facts)) (set (map first addresses)))\n    91\t          \"every node occurrence carries exactly one address fact\")\n    92\t      (is (= (count addresses) (count (set (map first addresses)))))\n    93\t      (is (every? #(contains? rows (nth % 2)) addresses))\n    94\t      (let [root-e (some (fn [[e a]] (when (= :yin/root a) e)) ast-facts)]\n    95\t        (is (some #(= [root-e :yin/address root] (subvec % 0 3)) addresses)\n    96\t            \"the root occurrence names the program's content address\")))\n    97\t    (testing \"m is a local metadata entity carrying the session provenance\"\n    98\t      (is (integer? meta-e))\n    99\t      (is (every? #(= meta-e (nth % 4)) (concat ast-facts addresses)))\n   100\t      (is (= {:db/op :db/assert\n   101\t              :yin.repl/session (:shell-token state)\n   102\t              :yin.repl/root root\n   103\t              :yin.repl/round 1}\n   104\t             (into {} (map (fn [[_ a v]] [a v])) meta-facts))))\n   105\t    (testing \"only code is indexed: no result or printed output\"\n   106\t      (is (not-any? #(= 3 (nth % 2))\n   107\t                    (filter #(= :yin/value (second %)) ast-facts))\n   108\t          \"the literal operands are 1 and 2; the result 3 appears nowhere\")\n   109\t      (is (= #{1 2}\n   110\t             (set (keep (fn [[_ a v]] (when (= :yin/value a) v)) ast-facts)))))))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(deftest the-round-publishes-covered-indexes-readable-from-dao-jing\n   114\t  (let [[state _] (evaluate (repl/create-state)\n   115\t                            [\"(def inc2 (fn [x] (+ x 2)))\" \"(inc2 40)\"])\n   116\t        {:keys [manifest-address content-store]} (:indexer state)\n   117\t        committed (into #{} (mapcat :datoms) (transactions state))]\n   118\t    (is (some? manifest-address))\n   119\t    (is (identical? content-store (:index-store state))\n   120\t        \"publication lands in the shell's dao.jing store\")\n   121\t    (testing \"the manifest's EAVT index holds every committed datom\"\n   122\t      (is (= 2 (count (transactions state))))\n   123\t      (is (= committed (set (index/read-datoms content-store manifest-address)))))\n   124\t    (testing \"each restored covered index holds the committed facts\"\n   125\t      (let [manifest (index/read-manifest content-store manifest-address)\n   126\t            restored (index/restored-indexes content-store manifest)]\n   127\t        (doseq [k [:eavt :aevt :avet :vaet]]\n   128\t          (is (= committed (set (seq (get restored k)))) (str k)))))\n   129\t    (testing \"the datoms read back from the store answer queries\"\n   130\t      (let [published (query/relation\n   131\t                        (index/read-datoms content-store manifest-address))\n   132\t            names (query/collect\n   133\t                    (query/q '[:find ?name\n   134\t                               :where [$ ?e :yin/type :variable]\n   135\t                               [$ ?e :yin/name ?name]]\n   136\t                             (query/current published)))\n   137\t            sessions (query/collect\n   138\t                       ;; the history view exposes m; current binds [e a v]\n   139\t                       (query/q '[:find ?session ?round\n   140\t                                  :where [?e :yin/root true ?t ?m]\n   141\t                                  [?m :yin.repl/session ?session ?t1 ?m1]\n   142\t                                  [?m :yin.repl/round ?round ?t2 ?m2]]\n   143\t                                (query/history published)))]\n   144\t        (is (every? (set (map first names)) '[yin/def x + inc2]))\n   145\t        (is (= #{[(:shell-token state) 1] [(:shell-token state) 2]}\n   146\t               (set sessions))\n   147\t            \"each program's root reaches its provenance through m\")))))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(deftest failed-expansions-add-nothing-raising-and-parking-programs-are-indexed\n   151\t  (testing \"a failed expansion forwards nothing, so nothing is committed\"\n   152\t    (let [[state [defined failed]]\n   153\t          (evaluate (repl/create-state)\n   154\t                    [\"(defmacro unless [c a b] (yin/if c b a))\"\n   155\t                     \"(unless 1 2)\"])]\n   156\t      (is (not (str/starts-with? defined \"Error\")))\n   157\t      (is (str/starts-with? failed \"Error: Macro expansion failed\"))\n   158\t      (is (= 1 (count (transactions state)))\n   159\t          \"only the defmacro program was committed\")))\n   160\t  (testing \"a program whose VM raises is still indexed\"\n   161\t    (let [[state [raised]] (evaluate (repl/create-state) [\"(nope 1)\"])]\n   162\t      (is (str/starts-with? raised \"Error: \"))\n   163\t      (is (= 1 (count (transactions state))))\n   164\t      (is (some? (get-in state [:indexer :manifest-address])))))\n   165\t  (testing \"a program whose VM parks is still indexed\"\n   166\t    (let [[state [text]] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type :stack})\n   167\t                                   [\"(require (quote mod))\"])]\n   168\t      (is (str/includes? text \"pending\"))\n   169\t      (is (some? (:pending-run state)))\n   170\t      (is (= 1 (count (transactions state)))))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(deftest every-evaluator-is-indexed-the-same-way\n   174\t  (doseq [vm-type (keys repl/vm-constructors)]\n   175\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   176\t      (let [[state [text]] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   177\t                                     [\"(+ 1 2)\"])]\n   178\t        (is (= \"3\" text))\n   179\t        (is (= 1 (count (transactions state))))))))\n   180\t\n   181\t\n   182\t(defn- small-medium\n   183\t  \"A ring medium of `capacity` and an observer attached at its oldest\n   184\t   position, as make-session composes program-out.\"\n   185\t  [capacity]\n   186\t  (let [writer (:dao.stream/handle\n   187\t                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   188\t                                ring/capacity-key capacity}))\n   189\t        descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor (stream/descriptor writer))\n   190\t        attach! (ring/make-attacher {(:dao.stream/identity descriptor) writer})]\n   191\t    {:writer writer\n   192\t     :observer (observer/attach attach! descriptor)}))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(deftest a-gap-on-the-index-reader-is-counted-never-indexed\n   196\t  (let [{:keys [writer observer]} (small-medium 2)\n   197\t        packets (mapv #(macro/ast->packet {:type :literal, :value %}) [1 2 3])\n   198\t        indexer (repl.index/make-indexer\n   199\t                  {:observer observer\n   200\t                   :session-token \"token\"\n   201\t                   :content-store (:index-store (repl/create-state))})]\n   202\t    (doseq [p packets] (stream/append! writer p))\n   203\t    (let [indexer' (repl.index/step indexer 1)\n   204\t          committed (mapv :dao.space/transaction\n   205\t                          (stream-values\n   206\t                            (get-in indexer' [:transactor :local-stream])))]\n   207\t      (is (= 1 (get-in indexer' [:observer :ingress-gaps])))\n   208\t      (is (= 2 (:transactions indexer')) \"only the retained packets\")\n   209\t      (is (= #{2 3}\n   210\t             (into #{}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | sed -n '45,58p;125,160p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md | sed -n '1024,1083p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | sed -n '45,58p;125,160p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md | sed -n '1024,1083p'\"","aggregated_output":"    45\tSide effects must appear as stream emissions.\n    46\tStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\n    47\tStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n    48\t\n    49\tA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\n    50\tof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\n    51\tsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\n    52\tstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\n    53\tthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\n    54\tanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\n    55\texists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\n    56\tthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\n    57\tand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\n    58\tbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\n   125\t## Architectural Commitments\n   126\t\n   127\t- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\n   128\t- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\n   129\t- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\n   130\t- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\n   131\t\n   132\t## Design Principles\n   133\t\n   134\tCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\n   135\tStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\n   136\t\n   137\t**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\n   138\tcomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\n   139\twithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\n   140\t\n   141\t- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\n   142\t  ordinary streams.\n   143\t- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\n   144\t  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\n   145\t- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\n   146\t- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\n   147\t  auto-index observer.\n   148\t- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\n   149\t  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\n   150\t\n   151\t**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\n   152\tcanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\n   153\tshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\n   154\t`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\n   155\tquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\n   156\tconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\n   157\tretired `:global` tag in\n   158\t[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\n   159\tcase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\n   160\t\n  1024\t### 6.5 What goes to the datom projection instead\n  1025\t\n  1026\tA tree also projects to datoms, `[e a v t m]` with tempids minted in\n  1027\tpreorder and one extra fact `[e :yin/address addr]` per node so the\n  1028\tprojection joins back to refs. This is the successor of `ast->datoms`\n  1029\t(`v2.cljc:372-482`) and is the *projection path* of §7.1. It exists for\n  1030\tthree queries the flat rows deliberately do not serve:\n  1031\t\n  1032\t+----------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1033\t| Query                                                                | Why the datom projection                                                                        |\n  1034\t+======================================================================+=================================================================================================+\n  1035\t| attribute-dimension queries with the attribute unbound, `[?e ?a ?v]` | a flat row has no attribute slot; \"every fact about this node\" is an EAV question               |\n  1036\t+----------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1037\t| `pull` and `entity-attrs` navigation (`query.cljc:715`, `:1481`)     | they navigate entity → attribute → value and reverse attrs                                      |\n  1038\t+----------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1039\t| scale indexing under covered indexes (`dao.space.index`)             | the covered-index publisher and `open-published!` are EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET over datoms           |\n  1040\t|                                                                      | (`query.cljc:452-476`)                                                                          |\n  1041\t+----------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1042\t\n  1043\tThe datom projection never becomes an identity: its `e` values are local,\n  1044\tand the only durable name in it is the `:yin/address` value.\n  1045\t\n  1046\t---\n  1047\t\n  1048\t## §7 The VM around it\n  1049\t\n  1050\t### 7.1 Load paths\n  1051\t\n  1052\tDirect row loading is primary. As `dao.stream` observers, evaluators receive batches natively from the stream. A batch on the program stream is the\n  1053\tcanonical row set of one tree (AST medium) or one canonical instruction\n  1054\tvector (code medium), and the evaluator's loader takes it as is:\n  1055\t\n  1056\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1057\t| Evaluator            | Loader input         | What loading does                                                                                                        |\n  1058\t+======================+======================+==========================================================================================================================+\n  1059\t| walker               | map AST              | natively reads map AST from stream topic without conversion — set `:program` and `:control` to the map.                    |\n  1060\t|                      |                      |                                                                                                                          |\n  1061\t|                      |                      |                                                                                                                          |\n  1062\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1063\t| semantic             | instruction vector   | validate (§7.5), decode positional operands into the image (the `case` of `semantic.cljc:563-593` reading `(nth tuple i)`|\n  1064\t|                      |                      | instead of attribute maps), store under `:code` with the address as the alias column UCF §7.3.4 requires                 |\n  1065\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1066\t| semantic,            | row set              | `lower` (§5.2) then the row above; composed by the composition exactly as `linearize/ast-loader` is today                |\n  1067\t| AST medium           |                      | (`linearize.cljc:269-286`, chosen in `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:63-68`)                                             |\n  1068\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1069\t\n  1070\tDatom-batch loading is the projection path: a batch of `:yin/*` datoms is\n  1071\tprojected to rows by the datom→row half of the §9.1 codec pair and then\n  1072\tloaded as above; a batch of `:yin.code/*` datoms is decoded to a vector\n  1073\tby UCF §7.3.4's projection rule and then loaded as above. The projection\n  1074\tpath exists for media that carry datoms and for the datom projection of\n  1075\t§6.5; it is not a second loader and it runs the same validator (§7.2).\n  1076\t\n  1077\t### 7.2 Conformance: both paths, one validator, one image\n  1078\t\n  1079\t**This section supersedes the sentence in UCF §7.3.4 that names the\n  1080\tprojection path as the reference path.** Under the owner's ruling the\n  1081\tdirect path is primary and the reference; the projection path is derived\n  1082\tfrom it. Everything else in §7.3.4 stands.\n  1083\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
