{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1435,1475p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc | sed -n '550,632p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1435\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1436\t                                  :clj Exception\n  1437\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n  1438\t                          {:error error}))]\n  1439\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n  1440\t\n  1441\t\n  1442\t(defn repl-state\n  1443\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  1444\t\n  1445\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  1446\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  1447\t   operation.\n  1448\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  1449\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n  1450\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n  1451\t   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n  1452\t   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n  1453\t   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n  1454\t   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n  1455\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).\"\n  1456\t  [state]\n  1457\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n  1458\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n  1459\t                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n  1460\t                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n  1461\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n  1462\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n  1463\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n  1464\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n  1465\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n  1466\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n  1467\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n  1468\t   :running? (:running? state)\n  1469\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n  1470\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n  1471\t   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1472\t              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n  1473\t                (mapv (fn [p]\n  1474\t                        {:name (:name p)\n  1475\t                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n   550\t\n   551\t(defn- append-ok!\n   552\t  \"Append one opaque payload to an intake stream; every stream/append!\n   553\t   must answer `:dao.stream/ok`, anything else throws with the result\n   554\t   attached.\"\n   555\t  [stream payload]\n   556\t  (let [result (stream/append! stream payload)]\n   557\t    (when-not (and (map? result) (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result)))\n   558\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"publish-index! stream append failed: \"\n   559\t                           (pr-str result))\n   560\t                      {:stream stream, :result result, :payload payload})))\n   561\t    result))\n   562\t\n   563\t\n   564\t(defn publish-index!\n   565\t  \"The transactor entry point, agent-side (docs/design/dao.jing.md,\n   566\t   Publication from an agent).\n   567\t\n   568\t   1. Snapshots the agent's local stream (snapshot-datoms) — fully, before\n   569\t      any publication append. Atomic transaction records are flattened here.\n   570\t   2. Builds the four covered indexes into a temporary recording content\n   571\t      handle through dao.data.btree.storage/kv-storage, so addresses are\n   572\t      minted by jing/materialize! and equal blobs deduplicate in\n   573\t      children-before-parent first-insertion order.\n   574\t   3. Appends every unique node blob in that recorded order, then the\n   575\t      manifest, all to exactly the intake stream selected from the pool.\n   576\t   4. Returns {:manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest) :manifest\n   577\t      manifest}.\n   578\t\n   579\t   The manifest address is derived from the manifest alone and never depends\n   580\t   on which intake stream carried it. A partial immutable prefix on a full\n   581\t   intake stream is acceptable and retry-safe: the manifest is always\n   582\t   appended last, so a :full failure can only have left node blobs.\n   583\t\n   584\t   Success acknowledges that every payload was appended to the selected\n   585\t   intake stream. It does not acknowledge that an asynchronous DaoJing\n   586\t   observer has materialized those payloads yet. Because the build starts at\n   587\t   the retained history's origin and reconstructs complete indexes,\n   588\t   local-stream must be on a complete-retention transport\n   589\t   (dao.stream.memory-log); the snapshot is complete before anything is\n   590\t   emitted.\n   591\t\n   592\t   Usage:\n   593\t     (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool)\n   594\t     (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool\n   595\t                     {:branching-factor n, :select-stream f})\n   596\t\n   597\t   opts: {:branching-factor n — max keys per node, at least 2 (default 512)\n   598\t          :select-stream f   — receives the pool and returns the intake\n   599\t                               stream to append to (default first)}\"\n   600\t  ([local-stream intake-pool] (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool nil))\n   601\t  ([local-stream intake-pool opts]\n   602\t   (let [branching (validate-branching! (:branching-factor opts 512))\n   603\t         intake (select-intake-stream! intake-pool (:select-stream opts first))\n   604\t         datoms (snapshot-datoms local-stream)\n   605\t         handle (recording-content-handle)\n   606\t         storage (bts/kv-storage handle {:branching-factor branching})\n   607\t         build-tree\n   608\t         (fn [cmp]\n   609\t           (bt/from-sequential cmp datoms {:branching-factor branching}))\n   610\t         trees {:eavt (build-tree eavt-cmp),\n   611\t                :aevt (build-tree aevt-cmp),\n   612\t                :avet (build-tree avet-cmp),\n   613\t                :vaet (build-tree vaet-cmp)}\n   614\t         root-addr (fn [tree]\n   615\t                     ;; an empty index has no root node; nil is the\n   616\t                     ;; explicit\n   617\t                     ;; \"nothing here\" (walk of nil => ())\n   618\t                     (when (seq datoms) (bt/store-tree tree storage)))\n   619\t         manifest {:indexes {:eavt (root-addr (:eavt trees)),\n   620\t                             :aevt (root-addr (:aevt trees)),\n   621\t                             :avet (root-addr (:avet trees)),\n   622\t                             :vaet (root-addr (:vaet trees))},\n   623\t                   ;; Covered indexes are sets. Their count must describe\n   624\t                   ;; the distinct tuples actually stored, not duplicate\n   625\t                   ;; occurrences in the source stream.\n   626\t                   :count (bt/count (:eavt trees)),\n   627\t                   :branching-factor branching}]\n   628\t     (doseq [[address bs] (:order @(:state handle))]\n   629\t       (append-ok! intake (jing/segment-value address bs)))\n   630\t     (append-ok! intake manifest)\n   631\t     {:manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest), :manifest manifest})))\n   632\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
